<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tomislav of Croatia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 910–928</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tomislav was the first ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> to be styled king, around 925. Originally Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-croatia">Dalmatian Croatia</a>, he fought off Hungarian incursions and united his land with Pannonian Croatia, and he was addressed as king in a papal letter of 925. In 926 his army defeated an invasion by the Bulgarian ruler Simeon I.</p></div>
